// RULE: W14, in the direction that over-promises. A function declaring
// `read@ledger_consistent` while reading a `bounded` view returns a stale answer and tells
// every caller it is fresh.
// WHY IT MATTERS: this was *accepted* until now, on the reasoning that a weaker read is
// covered by a stricter declaration. The direction is backwards: a read effect states the
// freshness of the result, not a permission the function asked for.
// EXPECT: NL0310
// STAGE: check
fn over_promise() -> Money<usd> ! { read@ledger_consistent } { stale_balance.get(1) }
